":"/en/usage/authoring-tools#data-editor--createedit-data","content":"Top &#x2A;*Export JSON…** — save as a `reactions`-format array"},"84":{"id":"/en/usage/authoring-tools-16","page_id":"/en/usage/authoring-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/authoring-tools#data-editor--createedit-data","content":"The key point is that **you don't type trigger/condition/effect types directly**.\nThe dropdowns expose only the names actually registered in the registry, so typos and unregistered types are blocked at the source.\nThe saved JSON is read by `JsonDataLoader` as is."},"85":{"id":"/en/usage/authoring-tools-17","page_id":"/en/usage/authoring-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/authoring-tools#data-editor--createedit-data","content":"> Authoring is UI, runtime consumption is data files — users never need to touch JSON directly."},"86":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","type":"page","content":"Core concepts","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/concepts"},"87":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-0","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts","content":"Triggers, conditions, effects, and the domain-agnostic data model."},"88":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-1","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/concepts#multiplication-into-addition","content":"Multiplication into addition"},"89":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-2","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/concepts#the-four-layers","content":"The four layers"},"90":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-3","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/concepts#reaction--trigger--condition--effect","content":"Reaction = trigger → condition → effect"},"91":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-4","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/concepts#integration-boundary","content":"Integration boundary"},"92":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-5","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/concepts#we-dont-use-typeof","content":"We don't use typeof"},"93":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-6","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#multiplication-into-addition","content":"Building a dedicated system for each domain (SkillSystem, MonsterSystem, …) means\nfilling in the `domain × behavior` matrix every time. AchReactive makes the **behavior pool\nshared by all domains**, turning this into `domain + behavior`."},"94":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-7","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#multiplication-into-addition","content":"Adding a new domain → 1 data class (0 system code)"},"95":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-8","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#multiplication-into-addition","content":"Reusing an existing behavior → 0 code, data only"},"96":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-9","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#multiplication-into-addition","content":"A genuinely new behavior → 1 function, then shared by all domains"},"97":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-10","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#the-four-layers","content":"The top two layers are provided by the package and don't change. You only fill in the bottom two layers."},"98":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-11","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#reaction--trigger--condition--effect","content":"Every domain is expressed in the same language."},"99":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-12","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#reaction--trigger--condition--effect","content":"The shape is identical even across different domains."},"100":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-13","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#reaction--trigger--condition--effect","content":"`add_modifier` is **one and the same code** whether a skill or an item uses it."},"101":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-14","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#integration-boundary","content":"The game only implements two interfaces."},"102":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-15","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#integration-boundary","content":"**`IEntity`** — `Id`, `Position`, `Stats` (StatSheet), `IsAlive`"},"103":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-16","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#integration-boundary","content":"**`IWorld`** — `Spawn`, `Collect`"},"104":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-17","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#integration-boundary","content":"Effects/conditions access `Source`/`Target`/`Targets`/`World` through the `ReactionContext`."},"105":{"id":"/en/usage/concepts-18","page_id":"/en/usage/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/concepts#we-dont-use-typeof","content":"When grouping multiple domains, we don't use a type-keyed service locator like `Dictionary<Type, object>`.\nEach `DataBase<T>` is **held explicitly**, and effects that need cross-domain references are\nsolved with manual registration + closure capture."},"106":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","type":"page","content":"Data and sources","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/data-sources"},"107":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-0","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources","content":"IData, DataBase, and JSON, CSV, and custom loaders."},"108":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-1","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/data-sources#idata-and-database","content":"IData and DataBase"},"109":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-2","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/data-sources#source-agnostic--idataloadert","content":"Source-agnostic — IDataLoader<T>"},"110":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-3","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/data-sources#json","content":"JSON"},"111":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-4","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/data-sources#csv","content":"CSV"},"112":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-5","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/data-sources#custom-sources","content":"Custom sources"},"113":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-6","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/data-sources#data-format-reactions","content":"Data format (reactions)"},"114":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-7","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#idata-and-database","content":"All domain data implements `IData` (= `string Id`). `DataBase<T>` is an in-memory index of\n`id → definition`, and **all domains share this single class generically**."},"115":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-8","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#source-agnostic--idataloadert","content":"No matter where you read data from, it goes through the same boundary, `IDataLoader<T>`. The package provides two implementations."},"116":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-9","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#json","content":"Based on Newtonsoft.Json, it reads a top-level array as is. (No wrapper class needed.)"},"117":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-10","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#csv","content":"Uses the first row as the header and converts each row with `ICsvMapper<T>`. Quotes, commas, and newlines are supported."},"118":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-11","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#csv","content":"`ICsvMapper<T>` implementations are usually generated by the Type Designer."},"119":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-12","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#custom-sources","content":"For binary, ScriptableObject, in-house formats, etc., you only need to implement `IDataLoader<T>`."},"120":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-13","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#custom-sources","content":"> JSON in the editor, CSV/Remote in production — you just **swap out the source**."},"121":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-14","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#data-format-reactions","content":"Domain data inherits from `EntityData`. The common fields are `id`, `stats`, and `reactions`."},"122":{"id":"/en/usage/data-sources-15","page_id":"/en/usage/data-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/data-sources#data-format-reactions","content":"`params` is an arbitrary key-value (`ParamBag`) that effects/conditions read with type conversion,\nlike `ctx.Params.Get<float>(\"power\")`."},"123":{"id":"/en/usage/extending","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","type":"page","content":"Extending","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/extending"},"124":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-0","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending","content":"New behaviors, new domains, and cross-domain connections."},"125":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-1","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/extending#adding-a-new-behavior","content":"Adding a new behavior"},"126":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-2","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/extending#path-a--attribute-recommended","content":"Path A — Attribute (recommended)"},"127":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-3","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/extending#path-b--manual-registration","content":"Path B — Manual registration"},"128":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-4","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/extending#adding-a-new-domain","content":"Adding a new domain"},"129":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-5","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/extending#cross-domain","content":"Cross-domain"},"130":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-6","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/extending#aot-il2cpp-caveat","content":"AOT (IL2CPP) caveat"},"131":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-7","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#path-a--attribute-recommended","content":"Write a static method annotated with `[Effect]`/`[Condition]`/`[Trigger]`, and `AutoRegister()`\ncollects it automatically from all assemblies. There is no wiring code."},"132":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-8","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#path-a--attribute-recommended","content":"The signatures are fixed."},"133":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-9","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#path-b--manual-registration","content":"Use this when you need DI, runtime state, or closures."},"134":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-10","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#adding-a-new-domain","content":"A new domain needs only **1 data class**. There is no system code."},"135":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-11","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#adding-a-new-domain","content":"`damage`/`add_modifier`, etc., reuse what skills already registered, as is → 0 lines of code.\nData classes and CSV mappers can be generated with the Type Designer."},"136":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-12","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#cross-domain","content":"When an effect needs to reference another domain's data, use **manual registration + closure capture**\ninstead of auto-registration to capture the relevant `DataBase<T>`. No type keys (typeof) are used."},"137":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-13","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#cross-domain","content":"> Recommendation: auto-register only pure behaviors that know nothing about domains; manually register only effects that need domain coupling."},"138":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-14","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#aot-il2cpp-caveat","content":"`AutoRegister()` is reflection-based, so methods may be stripped in IL2CPP builds.\nPreserve the assembly containing your behavior methods with `link.xml`."},"139":{"id":"/en/usage/extending-15","page_id":"/en/usage/extending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/extending#aot-il2cpp-caveat","content":"If you want to avoid reflection, you may use only &#x2A;*Path B (manual registration)**."},"140":{"id":"/en/usage/reactions","page_id":"/en/usage/reactions","type":"page","content":"Reactions and default behaviors","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/reactions"},"141":{"id":"/en/usage/reactions-0","page_id":"/en/usage/reactions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/reactions","content":"The ReactionEngine execution flow and the provided effects, conditions, and triggers."},"142":{"id":"/en/usage/reactions-1","page_id":"/en/usage/reactions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/reactions#execution-flow","content":"Execution flow"},"143":{"id":"/en/usage/reactions-2","page_id":"/en/usage/reactions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/reactions#reactioncontext","content":"ReactionContext"},"144":{"id":"/en/usage/reactions-3","page_id":"/en/usage/reactions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/reactions#